---
Title: underscores and tildes in addresses, and a percent in a link's URL
---

A bare address prints its underscores and tildes: https://example.com/a_b_c and
https://example.com/~me/page, <https://example.com/x_y~z> in angle brackets,
and www.example.com/w_x with no scheme.

A link written out keeps its URL's percent sign inside a footnote,[^note] in bold,
*[the bold link](https://example.com/u%20v)*, in bold italics,
**[the other](https://example.com/w%20x)**, and in a heading:

[^note]: See https://example.com/n_o~p and [the page](https://example.com/q%20r).

## Heading [linked](https://example.com/h%20i) and https://example.com/j_k

- https://example.com/l_m~n in a list

A written-out link's underscore and tilde are as they were:
[text](https://example.com/a_b~c).
